question:
Trace the output of the C snippet below:
```c
#include <stdio.h>
struct S {{
    int x;
    char y;
}};
int main() {{
    struct S s1 = {{10, 'A'}};
    struct S s2 = s1;
    s2.x = 20;
    printf("%d %c", s1.x, s1.y);
    return 0;
}}
```

Consider the following recursive C function with a static variable:
```c
int f(int n) {
    if (n <= 1) return 1;
    return n * f(n-1);
}
```
What is the return value of `f(3)`?
